**1. Reflection on Performance**

```
Objectives this quarter:
Migrate the BISS automation framework from Selenium to Playwright.
Make it ready to run in the CI/CD pipeline.

Playwright migration - on track
Built the new Playwright framework as a separate project, so the working Selenium suite kept running throughout.
Migrated one-to-one: the same feature files, step wording and 474 locators, so nobody writing tests had to relearn anything.
Running on Playwright: login, dashboard and the full end-to-end application journey (TC_03). Migrated and now in validation: My Clients, Create Client and Preliminary Checks (TC_07-TC_12, TC_18-20).
Solved blockers along the way: browser downloads blocked on department laptops, Angular Material dropdowns, and false FAIL results where all steps had passed.

Speed and reliability
Measured the suite from run logs and found around 40 seconds of fixed overhead per test case. Fixed the causes: the same browser is now reused across test cases, stale processes are cleared in under a second, and optional checks no longer wait 25 seconds for elements that are not there.
Added fail-fast, so a failed test case stops and the next one starts, and made reports match the real test result.

CI/CD readiness
Made the framework container-ready. Settings come from environment variables, credentials are injected at runtime (never in Git or the image), exit codes drive the build status, and the run can be split by test case.
Wrote the Docker/OpenShift pipeline design and a step-by-step guide for the DevOps team. Pipeline activation is with DevOps and will be the focus for Q4.

CPD Level expectations
Working at [CPD Level], I owned the technical design end to end, made architecture decisions (separate project, one-to-one migration, container-first), and turned the work into documentation others can follow.

Core Values
Ownership: went beyond the migration to fix performance and reporting accuracy.
Customer focus: every change aimed at faster, more trustworthy feedback on BISS releases for DAFM.
Collaboration: produced the CI/CD guide so the DevOps team could act without me.
Integrity: reports show handled failures separately instead of hiding them, and secrets were kept out of code.
```

